  "_origin" : "Messages CallAudioOnlyS0Test (audio-only calls S0, design AUDIO_ONLY_CALLS_DESIGN_2026-11-19 §5-§7, rulings R-1/R-2/R-3). `ring_cases`: `ring` is the text a verifier receives (the callring request, the push field `ring`, the live `signed_ring`); `expect.ok` = strict parse (unknown field / duplicate key refused), then the call signature under tkm-call/v1/ring for `aud`, then CallRschat.checkRing with `ring_to_max`. `expect.stage` is where THIS reference refuses (parse | signature | shape); a port must agree on `ok` and, for the shape cases, on `error` and `reason`. For an accepted ring: `canonical` = JCS of the object without sg, `signing_octets_hex` = ASCII(\"tkm-call/v1/ring\") || 00 || canonical, `sg` = Ed25519 (deterministic) over them, `push_ring` = JCS of the whole bean (CallRschat.pushRing), `media` = the verified field (null = a video ring). `body_cases`: `body` is the plaintext of a pairwise channel box as received; `expect.ok` = strict parse of CallChannelBodyBean; `canonical` / `plaintext_hex` = the bytes a sender seals (JCS, ASCII); `media` = the parsed field; `declaration` = what a RECEIVER takes (CallChannelBodyBean.declaredMedia): the media value ONLY when h == \"media\", else null — null also for h:\"media\" without media (no declaration = unknown cause); `known_value` is emitted only when h == \"media\" (else null): true for video/audio, false = the receiver shows «unknown cause». In `ring_cases` a JSON \"media\":null is the absent field (same canonical and push_ring as the ring without it). Keys: seeds are SHA3-256(ASCII(\"tkm-call/v1/vectors/identity/\" + name)) (CallTestKeys.identity).",
